        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="1233.8588976378" YPOS="27.087874015748" OwnPage="0" ItemID="205928656" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="134.645669291339" HEIGHT="1318.11023622047" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="1" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L134.646 0 L134.646 1318.11 L0 1318.11 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L134.646 0 L134.646 1318.11 L0 1318.11 L0 0 Z" gXpos="1233.8588976378" gYpos="27.087874015748" gWidth="76.120189628881" gHeight="1056.96849185058" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle LINESPMode="0" LINESP="11" FONT="Roboto Light" FONTSIZE="10"/>
                <ITEXT CH="01: Following conversion with mrconvert, the DWI scans are denoised, unringed, TOPUP and eddy corrected, biascorrected, and upsampled to 1.25mm"/>
                <ITEXT FEATURES="inherit superscript" CH="3"/>
                <ITEXT CH=" using the MRtrix3 pipeline"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="02: Lesion masks are registered to the subject DWI-space using a combination of mrconvert, FSL flirt, and mri_synthstrip"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="03: A brain mask is extracted from the upsampled DWI data using mri_synthstrip"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="04: Tissue responses are measured and averaged for each centre, then used to extract a white matter (FOD) skeleton from each subject, which is normalised using mtnormalise - also following the MRtrix3 pipeline"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="05: The FOD templates are averaged and non-linearly aligned, providing a population template"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="06: The subject FODs are aligned to the population template, and the subject-to-template warps are recorded"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="07: The subject-to-template warps are used to warp the subject-space brain masks to template space"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="08: Tract-specific ROIs are estimated from the population template by TractSeg"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="09: The subject-to-template warps are used to warp the subject-space DWI scans to template space"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="10: The subject-to-template warps are used to align lesion masks to template space"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="11: The tensor and kurtosis vectors are estimated from the templaet-space DWI scans using dwi2tensor"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="12: An inclusive population brain mask is generated from the intersection of template-space masks"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="13: A mask of fixels is generated from the combination of the FODs and the population brain mask"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="14: Fixels are extracted from the FODs, reoriented to align with the population template, and used to estimate FD and FC"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="15: A tractogram is computed using the population template, and sifted for parsimony and biological plausibility"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="16: Long- and short-range tractograms are seeded from lesion masks on the population template"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="17: Remaining fixel-metrics are computed from the template-space FODs"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="18: A connectivity matrix is built from the wholebrain tractogram"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="19: Fixel-metrics are smoothed using a connectivity-biased approach"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="20: Lesion networks are weighted by phenotype variables, and compared"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="21: Linear models are built and permutation tested to explore differences in fixel and scalar metrics between groups (with covariates)"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="22: Individual subject tract-specific measurements in fixel and scalar metrics are standardised and presented as deviations from expected values"/>
                <trail/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
